<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">State-directed industrialisation</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as model factories</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">State-directed industrialisation is economic development in which the government plans and finances industrial growth. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> established model factories, subsidised strategic industries and imported Western technology. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> also attempted state-led industrial projects.</p></div>
